    <description>&lt;p&gt;Initial feature set. Requires Julia 1.13 or later. Added Plain importance sampling and static multiple importance sampling with selectable weighting schemes. AMIS, N-PMC, DM-PMC, GR-PMC, LR-PMC, APIS, CAIS, and LAIS. First-order…&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    <content:encoded>&lt;h2&gt;ImportanceSamplers v0.0.1&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Initial feature set. Requires Julia 1.13 or later.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Added&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plain importance sampling and static multiple importance sampling with selectable weighting schemes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AMIS, N-PMC, DM-PMC, GR-PMC, LR-PMC, APIS, CAIS, and LAIS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First-order GRAMIS-CAIS with gradients and local covariance adaptation, distinct from the Hessian-based GRAMIS algorithm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spherical, diagonal, and factor Gaussian and Student-t proposals, uniform boxes, and independent Gamma and Laplace proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proposal banks, product proposals, and optional Distributions.jl integration. Adaptive support depends on the method and proposal family.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scalar and batch log targets, target contexts, and DensityInterface and LogDensityProblems integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Named parameters and identity, interval, positive, softplus, and simplex transforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explicit gradients and DifferentiationInterface-based CPU automatic differentiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reusable prepared samplers, adapted proposals, and target replacement through &lt;code&gt;retarget&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weighted moments and functionals, log-normalizer estimates, weight ESS, resampling, and sample provenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serial and threaded CPU execution, with explicit device transfer through MLDataDevices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optional CUDA, Metal, and Reactant execution. Supported methods, precision, and gradient routes vary by backend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tutorials, method guides, equation reproducers, and CPU/CUDA model comparisons with recorded environments and accuracy checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A density-ratio logo in SVG and PNG formats, used in the README and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The API is experimental. Backend and method restrictions are documented in the manual.&lt;/p&gt;
